## Summary

Added a `market` building kind and the `sellResource` trade function.

**`src/types.ts:4`** — extended the `BuildingKind` union with `"market"`.

**`src/buildings/registry.ts`** — registered `market: { cost: { wood: 20, stone: 15 }, requires: "storehouse" }` and gave it `category: "trade"` (added `"trade"` to the `BuildingCategory` union, which was the only place that needed it — `BUILDING_CATEGORY` is a full `Record<BuildingKind, ...>`, so the type union is only safe once every kind has a category).

**`src/sim/trade.ts`** (new) — `sellResource(settlement, resource, amount)`:
- Throws if no `market` is built.
- Sells `min(amount, held)` of the resource (never below 0), converting to stone at `floor(sold/2)`.
- Returns a new settlement via the existing `credit` helper.

**`src/sim/index.ts:11`** — exported `sellResource` alongside the other module exports.

Verification: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` (15 tests) passing, plus a runtime check of the 2:1 ratio, floor, never-below-0 cap, and the throw. No exhaustive `switch` over `BuildingKind` exists in the repo, so the new kind doesn't break anything else.


